<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Privacy manifest for the Gains app (Apple-required for App Store submission).

  Gains is LOCAL-FIRST: the user's health data stays on the device. The developer operates no server and
  collects nothing, so NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes is empty.

  AI egress (all of it on the USER's OWN BYOK OpenRouter key: the user sharing their own data with a
  provider they chose, not the developer collecting it). Two surfaces reach the network:
    1. Food logging, FoodAINutritionService, sends the food line the user typed.
    2. Workout logging, WorkoutParseService, sends the free-text workout the user typed.
  Both also carry the user's two formatting settings (calorie bias, micronutrient toggles). The food
  surface additionally has a VISION lane, FoodVisionService, which sends a JPEG the user shot: a meal
  photo, a nutrition label, or a restaurant menu, inline as base64 in the one request.

  What is NEVER sent: profile (age/height/weight), Whoop metrics, HRV, recovery, sleep, workouts other
  than the line being parsed, and any device or account identifier. The request carries only the user's
  own key plus a static HTTP-Referer / X-Title, see OpenRouterProvider in Sources/Services/AIProvider.swift.

  KEEP IN SYNC: the App Store Connect privacy "label" is where user-facing data-use disclosure lives, and
  the vision lane means PHOTOS are a disclosed data type there. This manifest covers only SDK collection +
  required-reason APIs, of which the one used is UserDefaults for the app's own storage.

  No tracking, no tracking domains. Required-reason API: UserDefaults (CA92.1, the app accesses info from
  itself, i.e. reads/writes its own defaults, never shared with other apps). Audited: no file-timestamp,
  disk-space, or system-boot-time required-reason APIs are used.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
    <false/>
    <key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
    <array/>
    <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
    <array/>
    <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
    <array>
        <dict>
            <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
            <string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults</string>
            <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
            <array>
                <string>CA92.1</string>
            </array>
        </dict>
    </array>
</dict>
</plist>
